<title>USA: Chiron compound fails Bayer trial.</title>
<headline>Chiron compound fails Bayer trial.</headline>
<dateline>EMERYVILLE, Calif. 1997-05-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chiron Corp said Wednesday its tumor necrosis factor (TNF) was found not to reduce mortality in septic shock patients.</p>
<p>The results were reported in a Phase III trial by Bayer AG, which licensed TNF, a monoclonal antibody, from Chiron.</p>
<p>Chiron would have earned an unspecified milestone payment from Bayer had the trials been successful.</p>
<p>Although earlier-stage trials had suggested the compound could be effective, Chrion said septic shock, in which infections go into the blood stream, has traditionally been very difficult to treat.</p>
<p>Bayer is continuing to test the TNF compound in other applications.</p>
</text>
